    </node>
    <node id="46c885603c8379e0748dc2de19e7319c77579b04f29d24bf42c50f82e8e17492">
      <data key="d0">The WSUD provisions within this chapter apply to new development and redevelopment within the area.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="80f3d042c7897897398f08b2f4201103af2b043a9ce8e6c1c5095b80ea22a30e">
      <data key="d0">to reduce potable water use, and treat stormwater so that the area reaches the relevant stormwater quality targets for stormwater reuse and/or stormwater entering receiving waters.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3ab4a658e6e834c4300c8350ee9a83b16b5a81e7b4e7689f25f45c71f53c0f69">
      <data key="d0">Specific developments are required to meet water conservation and stormwater quality targets.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1834f39584a29857536ff82a839533a30e0cd8f9aa54afcea3ccd79828210269">
      <data key="d0">the WSUD provisions within this chapter apply to new development and redevelopment within the area.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="46503da9de6b53adab16bfd679202118460afb3cf04c4fceda37e28a05131dbc">
      <data key="d0">All residential buildings are to demonstrate compliance with State Environmental Planning Policy - Building Sustainability Index (BASIX), as required.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1482589e6fa3e2fa94cb3c12e0bb869b35fec65a1bf2615609f2041ebe4d5d72">
      <data key="d0">All buildings not covered by the State Environmental Planning Policy - BASIX must meet minimum standards defined by the Water Efficiency Labelling and Standards (WELS) Scheme.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="eb4aae844ea93d1ae189701decf1bd1ef3235e7a8091fb1064fa04a4bb4342bb">
      <data key="d0">are to install rainwater tanks to meet all non-potable demands, including outdoor use, toilets, and laundry.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="607915d787debff7dfe784c3cda30df980df82292c5956a49ecc53a1238e2c9e">
      <data key="d0">are to incorporate passive cooling methods that rely on improved natural ventilation to supplement or preclude mechanical cooling.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="b8837414dc6f2255117c3c30be50e08155bbfd56703df6ea606383205ddbd0a6">
      <data key="d0">where cooling towers are used, they are: to be connected to a conductivity meter to ensure optimum circulation before discharge.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="e9fa51a21b85e109e555d2583cc81a5308afbcc5cecbad799ed8f806f1573eb2">
      <data key="d0">to include a water meter connected to a building energy and water metering system to monitor water usage.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
    </node>
