      <data key="d0">applicants</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="b17c22a241934f7eff9368db2a7d16d68cf294954151038001d250d17ffb4edb">
      <data key="d0">Building designs for new houses, alterations to houses, dual occupancies and residential flat buildings are required to comply with the BASIX State Environmental Planning Policy (SEPP).</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ac1ba775ac07812182f8e3f69f4d3a824567872a46c2f713d9f478d3ce770649">
      <data key="d0">Council is unable to approve a development application for residential development that does not achieve the minimum BASIX ratings.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="00702e906f71fb6cddd144087b0e158ef04665bb6c2d560c6433c1acca3fa47e">
      <data key="d0">A BASIX certificate is required to be submitted to Council with each development application and this certificate certifies that the dwelling proposal will meet the required environmental targets.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="37f36ca65d0b57caab2301bd45cc0d6dfb0b77d5fb065c84691c6500f1164fc4">
      <data key="d0">The Building Code of Australia (BCA) requires certain non-residential building types to demonstrate they will meet minimum criteria for reducing energy consumption.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d29d4b4516a5e5648bfca0ebebfc6956eb141b8839aab6b548e12a1d0dd3ca63">
      <data key="d0">Inner West Council encourages applicants to go beyond the requirements of BASIX, and to incorporate as many sustainable design principles as possible</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3e65d3614038c2972f1b523e02c0592bbc33b94f8c52cc4e072c12075f8b1367">
      <data key="d0">This compliance must be shown at Construction Certificate stage.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7a54861ea803d7631218c39c99846c099ff2003730e882f2209797d2f0f6d4bf">
      <data key="d0">Alterations and additions to existing buildings, when the extent of work exceeds 50 percent of the existing building area, are also affected.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="397a6d389d883f1d361872ea89201b211e27cc18b1f24653c95e43ef4b48deda">
      <data key="d0">In order to comply with the BCA energy requirements at the Construction Certificate stage, the design of new buildings will have to be resolved “upfront” at development application stage.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7cc5c9da75c84b5cbb88700d33c0718acbc567756ce9238bc45c5ed3abb4a353">
      <data key="d0">building designs</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="32e7ad3136454aa9c351bcb74a8ca27cb87f91b3e462269fb2f00f485cbbbbf3">
      <data key="d0">BASIX sets out requirements on how to achieve water conservation and energy efficiency targets for residential development.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">e3c989eaadbf1328063159724870ae92c4e77bfdfe917f9ef44cb71e0eaf2c5f</data>
    </node>
