      <data key="d0">Leichhardt DCP</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">31cd6a0dd0c9c423d376cc0bb414d3159305c7e34a3c7b7051c6ffc7659e364f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="767d936aa40867342caf448e52e2c4816d506bb1584e610f8eb32c90c54b29b0">
      <data key="d0">Development within that part of the site highlighted in red on the view cone on Figure G29 is to be limited to a maximum height of RL17.70.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">31cd6a0dd0c9c423d376cc0bb414d3159305c7e34a3c7b7051c6ffc7659e364f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0fa3dada4a9bca0662626013a08d6dae74cdf62b4a62e55f6c60d9351e2c664e">
      <data key="d0">Figure G29</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">31cd6a0dd0c9c423d376cc0bb414d3159305c7e34a3c7b7051c6ffc7659e364f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0e395fcaba889084e5e5f340d7fd9feadfb70e82c5606b8c7be8f9b2fd5f9b33">
      <data key="d0">Development along the Johnston Street frontage is to have a maximum wall height of $7 m$ (i.e. two storeys) above footpath level, with the exception of the existing commercial building.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">31cd6a0dd0c9c423d376cc0bb414d3159305c7e34a3c7b7051c6ffc7659e364f</data>
    </node>
