      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fcb47dc111253ef5ddf396b0a13ee16c454638255eb8ff7cdf1ba96b567df842">
      <data key="d0">RMS Guide to Traffic Generating Developments (2002)</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3f75e46b5ad88343946a950705bbe3f57e55a2aacc415e9535c51220d8800134">
      <data key="d0">parking provision rates</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fea1c36e20191d74a8e1550dae197721fed77b19c38598dc39533a2458253191">
      <data key="d0">This section of the DCP guides the provision of car and bicycle parking and their design for private developments.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="e6f7ae15a6e124399b9b170d494ea054712cfba8221fb338255d9d4b4ff996e4">
      <data key="d0">Parking policy is an important component of promoting sustainable transport and planning for liveable and economically viable communities.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0f52fd01b975c6bca33ae5519080e295a005e2ca675e4d3e040df827e8f4e730">
      <data key="d0">To provide for current and future demand for bicycle parking and to ensure bicycle parking is well designed and located.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="e286983d0348904cb696748c21634001057009120b9f7e35ab8839422fc4e044">
      <data key="d0">In larger developments, and in some smaller developments where appropriate, a key action for improved management of parking is prioritising targeted users of parking space - for efficiency, equity and environmental reasons.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="35fc016a47582fe996d9ba1a663238d58a5aa0cf3c516f222c06ebebc98aa9c4">
      <data key="d0">It prescribes different car parking provision rates for three sub-sections of the LGA - highly accessible areas, moderately accessible areas and least accessible areas.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="a7abb556f9f042cd921f4b0de83c372446513519c83a6ba08b95f13504537999">
      <data key="d0">To balance the need to meet car parking demand on-site to avoid excessive spillover on to streets , with the need to constrain parking to maintain the area’s compact urban form and promote sustainable transport.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="dacba3a339506831c06a611f25d965a9e42182270a088af9ab5ba1b4e838f11b">
      <data key="d0">Car parking rates are most constrained in Parking Area 1 and least constrained in Parking Area 3.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ab24a584e7a2cbe6bcaa0a74df35c409b2a28962229e8cc06639122e159853ac">
      <data key="d0">For bicycles, provision rates are prescribed uniformly across the where this DCP applies.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0b71552edd2bf433255f8384c3795b8bf00d9aba12a6412df5e75c2e4cc395db">
      <data key="d0">Contemporary policies also meet current demand and allow for future demand for bicycle parking a nd parking for carshare and environmental vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="f3ae50960338984e4d427c80f3861277d3af0983c2c6043fb3afb7bc086a673c">
      <data key="d0">RMS Guide to Traffic Generating Developments ( 2002 ), which provides guidance on parking provision rates, whilst re cognising the need to reduce those rates in accessible areas in the interests of applying travel demand management principles,</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="34e26647caec9501fe44a807de3bc9ee66d24e3b3deb843182b00e93fd0b4216">
      <data key="d0">private developments</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="69dd23a35dfea168e45e280ae61d101a00f8675209ebcde12102f3a528c7d6e2">
      <data key="d0">It prescribes different car parking provision rates for three sub-sections of the LGA - highly accessible areas (Parking Area 1), moderately accessible areas (Parking Area 2) and least accessible areas (Parking Area 3).</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="da4ec0df8bb13ef87582cee66e0066551b993ff2b81b8a20dadbca101f1498bb">
      <data key="d0">Parking Area 2</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="57494b8dc111af837c2c169f99571d9653ed82fe31d42771d20a7cac20ff3031">
      <data key="d0">bicycles</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5bb08b7f7c4781ef765b1157ab188502ab85b1011d01833f8223a5ec2e4bca26">
      <data key="d0">To balance the need to meet car parking demand on-site to avoid excessive spillover on to streets, with the need to constrain parking to maintain the area’s compact urban form and promote sustainable transport.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2a384fbaf0fd5ff12bebd526372a170a88c3965ef7f30f993e1cb9eb7d8df6</data>
    </node>
