      <data key="d0">high solid walls and fences</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2c5e34862e8f9d027e851f3f6d50c9a72f272c6b352d7c7b82cab489d03065bc">
      <data key="d0">aluminium panel fencing</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="be9bbc85b460c59d8a704ee7e4bab7d5c0bdced732479f42cc122499bdd3242a">
      <data key="d0">Specific detail for fencing in heritage conservation areas is provided in Part 8 (Heritage) of this DCP.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="977b1c679b8467d5b596ffb6f2ffc177073b0d79bcca3bc8c2107c8fe6d36680">
      <data key="d0">NB Specific detail for fencing in heritage conservation areas (HCAs) is provided in Part 8 (Heritage) of this DCP.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6fc7078b0593ba7368601639c3272d0c7b609a125e480ced1b9b5e7f6134f160">
      <data key="d0">Modifications to the fence of a heritage item, period building or within a heritage conservation area must be designed in a manner which contributes to the historic style of the building and streetscape context.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="66d1dd2eef4fa209b9368f670f22a6410fe96330ce04f500596872b2f976fd76">
      <data key="d0">Existing fences must be retained where they are consistent with the period style of the building.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="f9bbd73d4fd0029c3624b80ae91e7492495e4db157d7c3eb844eae301f28b028">
      <data key="d0">Any new fences must be consistent with the traditional designs used in the area, but using simpler detailing.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="bd605a08f58eb0e9042e406b7606f2546e8045a0cdc6707863c1df6f567617be">
      <data key="d0">Fences over 1.2 metres high are generally inappropriate as they reduce visibility of the garden setting and the heritage item or period building.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7eafb227705ff85e0062d58933fa561d49a57ed4060cbd1982ded53f40d42aa2">
      <data key="d0">On sloping sites, fences may rise to a maximum 1.5 metres before stepping down to 1.2 metres or less.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="04599f96a9551c98f9bef1d09c1385afb8eabc968c740467f806fb0be97f1ad6">
      <data key="d0">High solid walls and fences must be avoided as they detract from the streetscape and impede passive surveillance.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0968133aaf6b10e5b109a685472007f1545c99edb167ee62515b8948169c3be6">
      <data key="d0">New fences must be finished in dark or recessive materials and surfaces, and aluminium panel fencing must be avoided.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="55680e6804916782e96f5dc1b4ca9983c2b191a602a3d7b150c4264bf5408987">
      <data key="d0">Specific detail for fencing in heritage conservation areas is provided in Part 8 of this DCP.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">74fa61fe3e659a2e3515896a5479b2ca83762a41492b2ea3212a960bf318bd90</data>
    </node>
