      <data key="d0">driveways or garages</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fde82fd3bb86bba57ca16fc216a0624cef72001d17db535d67e090c53b0e8d0e">
      <data key="d0">view of the development</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="b16ad0026efc31f6da6bcb9b8eee7aadcd2bb2c6e97c458687f76d2d10c02ec9">
      <data key="d0">Clause 4.2 provides core controls and objectives relevant to multi dwelling housing and residential flat buildings.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="00fb3b5d6fac563b4544ed0f6cda3a59ca62b9e2ed357cfb629479798201f132">
      <data key="d0">It must be consulted in conjunction with other relevant sections of the DCP that provide applicable controls and objectives like parking, landscaping, fencing or solar access.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="c60f2f3910b38da4ed97550bd9cb32eaededf393db88bebb4a9a965d7243ec5b">
      <data key="d0">State Environmental Planning Policy (Building Sustainability Index: BASIX) 2004 (BASIX SEPP) requires new residential developments to be energy and water efficient.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1bb7c271021395d22d593c384cfb2e798ad32d6d99c9a12eded0675299cf6bf1">
      <data key="d0">To maintain a reasonable level of amenity for neighbours by ensuring development has minimal impact on neighbouring/adjoining properties in terms of building dominance (bulk and scale), overshadowing and privacy (both visual and acoustic).</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="e87645ec413cd246220307f60a29dd8e4bd4c28ab40be4214763f0d84fae4edc">
      <data key="d0">To consider building location, design and car parking in order to maximize use of public transport.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="9da3ff8a372eeeb14e21b93d1151a88b669830b09e56f68ba1511a0fc623462d">
      <data key="d0">Ensure new development maintains the same setback and enhances the streetscape character of the locality,</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="21c1cb71499d91baf29a3e3a67ec2d508126343a215e82a5283ada3930883120">
      <data key="d0">Ensure driveways or garages do not dominate the view of the development from the street and consider alternative modes of transport and car share options to reduce on-site parking.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="90aedddf0ac48543974165e3b461676dbf1637fe517c905da022478b8777a1b8">
      <data key="d0">Section 4.2 provides core controls and objectives relevant to multi dwelling housing and residential flat buildings.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">4ed2651847721a50ee2c951d40f7716a6b49625f7686553586004effc61aa368</data>
    </node>
