    <node id="e442ebd4f52e9d02b36e67e052f3d845b9b271ed1b97ce0dfaa02684b0c1f7c6">
      <data key="d0">the operations of the shopping centre</data>
      <data key="d1">entity</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8d70e72c8797cfe84646023506549ae63ea9882801ff08c9fe092da36a468429">
      <data key="d0">Part of the brick factory wall was retained and is still visible along Victoria Road.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="158ba67e8f0619f0bbd7f3873f0fd6b32a7f044612bcce2ae31503e69a71d081">
      <data key="d0">The Mill House, built about 1860 and occupied by the Vicars family, was incorporated in the redevelopment.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8bb2843fe7f05030d16166e017dfd7048370b2272ca6c9edaa4ebbea4b84183a">
      <data key="d0">Pedestrian access is also provided from the rooftop car parking areas down into the centre.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6d7c49eb1491c14017ff9aced5656778960a16171dcc7a39fb9d7cca7dae4694">
      <data key="d0">Two vehicle access ramps accessed off Smidmore and Murray Street provide car access to the roof top parking.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="48f2b383cb8eb6eb6dff8b03a051083a8a1058f1be95952ea52f67a9e2589fdc">
      <data key="d0">The site on the southern side of Smidmore Street from the Marrickville Metro shopping centre is a large industrial lot, containing a two storey industrial warehouse development built to the boundary and associated car parking.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="55a24ff7aedaadedbf143e501202e44c6956f8b9615f2eaa7084f1f074adef13">
      <data key="d0">The block to the east contains a mix of large and smaller lots, predominantly containing two storey industrial buildings and associated car parking.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="eec5149495ba02ee28e90538fbd2899bde68742658cbb6a2c9c3ce24928e91b0">
      <data key="d0">Roads in this precinct tend to be quite narrow, with time restricted parking on both sides of the streets.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="f630a3732ced1d45fca67131c723b937b1e0c68eb2e691ba5a7fa7f413b3a3b1">
      <data key="d0">The operations of the shopping centre have the potential to impact on the amenity of residential areas by way of noise and other emissions, parking and traffic generation.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="9aa044fca54720638853e337a71540c894cdb0dd91f1deff57e0698a072d978c">
      <data key="d0">The precinct does not contain any Heritage Conservation Areas.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">f6a65e4aed0cc496000b4749a6f8a01439971ee806a6f21e52ca00362ac450ce</data>
    </node>
