    <node id="e5852e5cdfc12d22f469eeffb3aaee7b32d28cbadc811b8c02edd5a12f1f642e">
      <data key="d2">e5852e5cdfc12d22f469eeffb3aaee7b32d28cbadc811b8c02edd5a12f1f642e</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 12 Signs and Advertising Structures

Clause 2.12.4.6 - height_limit (development_control): Signage on high-rise buildings (in excess of 15 metres)

Clause 2.12.2 - other (development_control): Any underawning sign in excess of 2500mm x 400mm

Clause 2.12.2 - height_limit (development_control): Signs at a lower level than 2600mm above the footpath

Clause C3 - heritage (heritage): Where original sign panels have been incorporated into the parapet of the building facade, these must be retained

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7de7863e3eb097534f36032c7ce77ac48ec8f29b2dde6a862ab3a70205d5bb1c">
      <data key="d2">7de7863e3eb097534f36032c7ce77ac48ec8f29b2dde6a862ab3a70205d5bb1c</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 13 Biodiversity

Clause C1 - other (environmental_protection): Development on land identified on the Biodiversity Map as Bandicoot Protection Area, provided in Appendix 3, may be required to undertake an assessment of significance.

Clause C2 - other (environmental_protection): Development on land identified on the Biodiversity Map as Wildlife Corridor, provided in Appendix 3, must incorporate native vegetation as part of any landscaping works.

Clause C3 - other (development_control): Buildings must be located to provide an outlook to public open space without appearing to privatise that space.

Clause C4 - other (development_control): Development must provide a visual transition between open space, bushland reserves or other public spaces and buildings, including avoiding abutting public open space with back fences.

Clause C5 - other (development_control): Development must protect views to and from public open spaces.

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="59a9fc5eb910b62893713973b3f90a5833729099846f311073f98f92b8ea680e">
      <data key="d2">59a9fc5eb910b62893713973b3f90a5833729099846f311073f98f92b8ea680e</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 14 Unique Environmental Features

Clause 2.14.2 - other (development_control): Development adjoining public open space must be set back from open space and be of a height and scale appropriate to the unique environmental qualities of the area.

Clause 2.14.5 - other (development_control): Development within the scenic protection area must be:
i. Designed and located to minimise potential adverse environmenta impact. This is particularly important where properties are within a foreshore area or where the land is flood affected (see maps in Section 2.22 – Flood Management);
ii. Of a scale compatible with the character, landscape and scenic qualities of the area;
iii. Of minimal visual impact when viewed from any adjoining public open space; and
iv. Where adjoining public open space provides a visual transition between open space and avoids abutting public open space with high, blank or solid fences (such as timber paling fences without openings or corrugated fencing).

Clause 2.14.5 - other (development_control): Sandstone cliffs, outcrops and overhangs must be retained in situ and integrated into the design of new development.

Clause 2.14.5 - other (environmental_protection): Any plantings are to enhance fauna habitat and to be local species endemic to the area.

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84">
      <data key="d2">21f316011e29c1f84bb215923d2a8f81b2db15ee4b8e5de33bbcefc564d66b84</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 17 Water Sensitive Urban Design

Clause 2.17 - other (development_control): The WSUD provisions within this chapter apply to new development and redevelopment within the area and aim to:  • Reduce potable water use; and Treat stormwater so that the area reaches the relevant stormwater quality targets for stormwater reuse and/or stormwater entering receiving waters.

Clause 2.17.2 - other (development_control): Specific developments are required to meet water conservation and stormwater quality targets that have been established for land where this DCP applies.

Clause 2.17.3 - other (development_control): All residential buildings are to demonstrate compliance with State Environmental Planning Policy - Building Sustainability Index (BASIX), as required.

Clause 2.17.3 - other (development_control): All buildings not covered by the State Environmental Planning Policy - BASIX: i. that are installing any water use fittings must meet minimum standards defined by the Water Efficiency Labelling and Standards (WELS) Scheme. Minimum WELS ratings are 4 star dual-flush toilets, 3 star showerheads, 4 star taps (for all taps other than bath

Clause 2.17.3 - other (development_control): are to install rainwater tanks to meet all non-potable demands, including outdoor use, toilets, and laundry (for child care centres, this water is to be used for irrigation and toilet flushing only).

Clause 2.17.3 - other (development_control): are to incorporate passive cooling methods that rely on improved natural ventilation to supplement or preclude mechanical cooling (refer Section 2.16.5.6).

Clause 2.17.3 - other (development_control): where cooling towers are used, they are:

a. to be connected to a conductivity meter to ensure optimum circulation before discharge.

Clause 2.17.3 - other (development_control): to include a water meter connected to a building energy and water metering system to monitor water usage.

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5749edd7368b578efeea00cd0949ded397b1bf519708601446f088cb6223a7a7">
      <data key="d2">5749edd7368b578efeea00cd0949ded397b1bf519708601446f088cb6223a7a7</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 18 Landscaping and Open Spaces

Clause 2.18 - other (environmental_protection): Any new development must preserve and protect any existing trees on site.

Clause 2.18.1 - other (environmental_protection): To minimise the extent of hard paved areas and facilitate rainwater infiltration.

Clause 2.18.1 - other (development_control): To encourage green roofs and green walls particularly for large scale developments.

Clause 2.18.3 - other (development_control): A landscape plan and maintenance schedule must be submitted with any development application for residential, commercial and industrial development that requires landscaping.

Clause 2.18.3 - other (development_control): d. Use of mulch or similar treatments of garden beds with mulch depth not less than 100mm

Clause 2.18.3 - other (development_control): xiv. Any court walls facing a communal area or public place or road (that must be constructed of a material similar in type and colour to that used for the development found on site); and

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="337f42c94de20ff6f5502760a8af2637b4825945eaae1901a16864899bee2787">
      <data key="d2">337f42c94de20ff6f5502760a8af2637b4825945eaae1901a16864899bee2787</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 25 Stormwater management

Clause # 2.25 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): The flow of stormwater from developments needs to be managed so as to negate or reduce to an acceptable frequency the possibility of flooding buildings and/or the danger to life at any location, through the storage of stormwater where appropriate in developments and the control of major development drainage systems.

Clause # 2.25.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To protect the urban environment from the effects of otherwise uncontrolled surface stormwater flows resulting from infrequent (and lesser) storm events.

Clause # 2.25.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To minimise or negate disruption and/or danger to both pedestrian and vehicular traffic that may be caused by otherwise uncontrolled surface stormwater flows resulting from frequent storm events.

Clause # 2.25.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To protect the quality of receiving waters, adjacent and downstream land-use and the rights of adjacent and downstream landowners.

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): On Site Detention	Yes (3, 6)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): On Site Retention	Yes (3,8)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Gravity Pipe System Required	Yes (4)

Clause # 2.25.2 - other (development_control): Pump System Permitted	No (4)

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="0a8debeb73ef9421193d58cf2b2f27bc0e0fa2c80b37bbfb3ee41c7ed01d32d4">
      <data key="d2">0a8debeb73ef9421193d58cf2b2f27bc0e0fa2c80b37bbfb3ee41c7ed01d32d4</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 3 Site Context Analysis

Clause 2.3 - setback (development_control): Front setbacks and front projections; • Side setbacks

Clause 2.3 - height_limit (development_control): Eaves height

Clause 2.3.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Minimise overshadowing, loss of privacy and views

Clause 2.3.3 - other (development_control): The site and context analysis must demonstrate that the development will integrate within the streetscape when considering scale, proportion and massing.

Clause 2.3.3 - other (development_control): The site and context analysis must demonstrate that the building is well proportioned, both as an individual element and within the streetscape.

Clause 2.3.3 - other (development_control): The site and context analysis must demonstrate that the building will sit comfortably with surrounding buildings in terms of its massing.

Clause 2.3.3 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Any endangered ecological community (EEC), significant trees or other vegetation (including any unique environmental features) and any other existing trees upon the site or close to the boundaries with adjoining sites

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="902f4a45c64b806594f7392b51ce8dafb2859a37359cb64a6e874f40ac8424d0">
      <data key="d2">902f4a45c64b806594f7392b51ce8dafb2859a37359cb64a6e874f40ac8424d0</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 5 Equity of Access and Mobility

Clause 2.5.1 - parking (development_control): To provide an adequate supply of car parking facilities for use by people with a disability.

Clause 2.5.3 - other (development_control): When assessing a development application Council must take into account the following matters as relevant to the application:
i. The provision for ease of use and comfort through appropriate gradients, rest areas, circulation space and user friendly entrances;
ii. Safety measures, including contrasting colours for points of danger, slip resistant travel surfaces and appropriate positioning of street furniture, public art installations, signage or any other obstacles, including those in the public domain;
iii. Legible design and way finding features, such as signs and international symbols and indicators, to assist in determining the location of handrails, guard-rails and tactile indicators where relevant;
iv. Opportunities for access through principal entrances of commercial buildings, pub...

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
