      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 4.1 Low Density Residential Development

Clause 4.1 - land_use_zoning (land_use_zoning): LOWDENSITY RESIDENTIAL DEVELOPMENT

Clause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To provide more details on the residential standards contained in Marrickville Local Environmental Plan 2011 (MLEP 2011).

Clause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To maintain and encourage compatible architectural styles within residential areas.

Clause 4.1.1 - other (environmental_protection): To encourage residential development which is sensitive to the local environment, socially responsive and which promotes a safe living environment and makes better use of existing infrastructure.

Clause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To ensure the impact of urban housing on the amenity of surrounding properties and the streetscape is a prime and initial consideration in the preparation and assessment of development proposals.

Clause 4.1.1 - heritage (development_control): To encourage restoration and sympathetic alterations and additions to residential period buildings in a manner that retains and enhances their architectural character and streetscape presentation.

Clause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To require high quality urban design and accessible and adaptable accommodation.

Clause 4.1.1 - other (development_control): To encourage innovative design that positively responds to the character and context of the locality.

