    <node id="eebc6e25c643d3f5ea65901f10dd71ea1ea090de9ab9d6032c7026cab0aeb130">
      <data key="d2">eebc6e25c643d3f5ea65901f10dd71ea1ea090de9ab9d6032c7026cab0aeb130</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 0 Introduction

Clause Part 9 - zoning (land_use_zoning): Part 9 of this DCP divides the land where this DCP applies into 47 planning precincts.

Clause Part 9 - other (development_control): Each planning precinct has its own distinct character and provides an important contextual basis for establishing appropriate types of development in association with other controls within the DCP.

Clause Part 9 - other (development_control): Each precinct has an existing and desired future character to guide development within the area.

Clause Part 9 - other (development_control): Planning controls and objectives have been applied to precinct-specific areas and site-specific areas (through masterplans) to assist in achieving the desired future character.

Clause Part 9 - heritage (development_control): Heritage conservation areas if located within a precinct are referenced.

Clause 9.35 - zoning (land_use_zoning): Parramatta Road (Commercial Precinct 35)

Clause 9.36 - zoning (land_use_zoning): Petersham (Commercial Precinct 36)

Clause 9.37 - zoning (land_use_zoning): King Street and Enmore Road (Commercial Precinct 37)

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8b6ff4ee7d780c45970af270220cdc8f23ac0166ecf53bbc5d1dfca515b7cc94">
      <data key="d2">8b6ff4ee7d780c45970af270220cdc8f23ac0166ecf53bbc5d1dfca515b7cc94</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 1 Lewisham North Precinct 1

Clause 9.1.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.

Clause 9.1.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect the identified heritage items within the precinct.

Clause 9.1.2 - height_limit (development_control): To maintain distinctly single storey streetscapes that exist within the precinct.

Clause 9.1.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect significant streetscapes and/or public domain elements within the precinct including landscaping, fencing, open space, sandstone kerbing and guttering, views and vistas and prevailing subdivision patterns.

Clause 9.1.2 - environmental_protection (development_control): To ensure that new development considers all potential impacts to biodiversity.

Clause 9.1.2 - zoning (development_control): To preserve the predominantly low density residential character of the precinct.

Clause 9.1.2 - parking (development_control): To ensure that the provision and location of off-street car parking does not adversely impact the amenity of the precinct.

Clause 9.1.4 - other (development_control): New development should address the GreenWay Corridor, recognising the space as an active frontage with substantial visual and environmental benefits; as well as an active transport corridor, and provide opportunities for street activation and/or public art and animation.

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="281f9b9327302b3b395dfc9e224e53bc1c462fb1c2911b1d66e18eb6396f32e5">
      <data key="d2">281f9b9327302b3b395dfc9e224e53bc1c462fb1c2911b1d66e18eb6396f32e5</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 10 Dulwich Hill North

Clause 9.10.1 - heritage (heritage): The precinct contains a heritage listed water board site in Weston Street which is substantially vacant except for a small brick building. The former Waratah flour mills and associated buildings (also heritage items) along the railway line are land mark buildings within this precinct and can be seen from a number of streets.

Clause 9.10.1 - other (land_use_zoning): The land-use pattern of the precinct is predominantly low density residential areas with some medium density development.

Clause 9.10.1 - setback (development_control): Front setbacks are generally consistent within each street despite the variety of buildings styles. A setback of 2 metres to 4 metres is the most common.

Clause 9.10.1 - parking (development_control): In areas of the precinct where off street parking is provided it is most frequently a side drive to a hardstand/carport behind the building line.

Clause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.

Clause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect the identified Heritage Items within the precinct.

Clause 9.10.2 - other (land_use_zoning): To preserve the predominantly low density residential character of the precinct.

Clause 9.10.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To ensure that new development considers all potential impacts to biodiversity.

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
    <node id="656a66f97b9376208aa4511dd0328416e211f846df84c8f5ea4aa363def2d893">
      <data key="d2">656a66f97b9376208aa4511dd0328416e211f846df84c8f5ea4aa363def2d893</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 11 Hoskins Park Precinct 11

Clause 9.11.1 - heritage (heritage_protection): This precinct also contains the Hoskins Park &amp; Environs Heritage Conservation Area.

Clause 9.11.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): It is essential that development within the precinct considers the potential impacts to biodiversity including native fauna (including Threatened Species and Endangered Populations); native vegetation (including Endangered Ecological Communities); and habitat elements (including their condition, structure, function, connectivity and disturbance).

