    <node id="53c13b983665ff26d3da688f01dce36924ff8f47738cc075f3d25157128dfe1a">
      <data key="d2">53c13b983665ff26d3da688f01dce36924ff8f47738cc075f3d25157128dfe1a</data>
      <data key="d0">Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/leichhardt/Leichhardt DCP 2013 - 13 - Appendix A Glossary - with IWLEP 2022 amendments.pdf

Clause APPENDIX A - other (development_control): Amenity means the enjoyment of the environment whether by the community or an individual arising from the day to day use of property including dwellings or publicly accessible land, community facilities or open space and includes, but is not limited to, the enjoyment of: 
a. Sunlight, privacy and views; and b. Residential and community life free from nuisance arising from the emission of noise, vibration, smell, fumes, smoke, vapour, steam, soot, ash, dust, waste water, waste products or grit.

Clause APPENDIX A - heritage (development_control): Conservation may, according to circumstance, include the processes of: retention or reintroduction of a use; retention of associations and meanings; maintenance, preservation, restoration, reconstruction, adaptation and interpretation; and will commonly include a combination of more than one of these.

Clause APPENDIX A - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Contaminated land means land in, on or under which any substance is present at a concentration above the concentration at which the substance is normally present in, on or under (respectively) land in the same locality, being a presence that presents a risk of harm to human health or any other aspect of the environment.

Clause APPENDIX A - heritage (development_control): Contributory item means a building in a Conservation Area that is not individually listed as a heritage item but by virtue of age, scale, materials, details, design style or intactness is consistent with the conservation area, and therefore reinforces its heritage significance.

Clause APPENDIX A - heritage (development_control): Cultural significance means aesthetic, historic, scientific, social or spiritual value for past, present or future generations.

Clause APPENDIX A - other (development_control): Flood certificate means a certificate obtained from Council which provides flooding information for the area in the vicinity of a particular property including peak water levels, depths and flow rates for the 100 year ARI and peak water levels for the Probable Maximum Flood event.

Clause APPENDIX A - other (development_control): Flood control lot means a lot identified as a flood control lot on the maps in Appendix E of this Development Control Plan (DCP). Also referred to as: Flood Hazard Area as defined in the Building Code of Australia (BCA) Note: All flood control lots are also within flood hazard areas as defined by the BCA.

Clause APPENDIX A - other (development_control): Floodplain means an area of land which is subject to inundation by floods up to and including the probable maximum flood event, that is, flood prone land.

</data>
      <data key="d1">passage</data>
    </node>
