      <data key="d0">Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/Marrickville/Marrickville DCP 2011 - 2 12 Signs and Advertising Structures.pdf

Clause 2.12 - other (development_control): This section of the DCP specifies Council’s objectives and requirements for the erection and display of advertising signs. These provisions are intend ed to protect the significant characteristics of retail/commercial strips, neighbourhoods, buildings, streetscapes, vistas and the skyline.

Clause 2.12 - other (development_control): Advertising signs clearly indicate  retail and commercial uses, and contribute to lively retail strip s. However, too much signage creat es visual clutter, detracts  from the  streetscape quality and reduces the effectiv eness of advertising .

Clause 2.12.1 - other (development_control): To ensure all advertisi ng achieve s a high level of design quality and is compatible  with the architectural design of the host building, the character of the streetscape and the size and juxtaposition of other signs in the immediate vicinity.

Clause 2.12.1 - other (development_control): To ensure signage does not dominate o r detract from the arc hitectural features of the building  and from the white -way lighting found along some retail strips.

Clause 2.12.1 - other (development_control): To ensure advertising does not cause amenity  loss, or have a detrimental effect on the natural or built environment or the safety, appearance or efficiency of any public area.

Clause 2.12.1 - other (development_control): To ensure the location and design of signs are consistent with road safety principles.

Clause 2.12.1 - other (development_control): To ensure the use of corporate logos, colour and illumination schemes in signage are compatible  with the architecture of the ho st building and do not adversely impact upon the local streetscape.

Clause 2.12.1 - other (development_control): To ensure signage retains the visual prominence and integrity of the roof and silhouette form of the business centre.

