Clause 9.15.1 - setback (development_control): Front setbacks vary throughout the precinct with common se tbacks of less than 2 metres for dwellings that are predominantly Victorian and Federation era and 2 -4 metre se tbacks for Federation and Inter -War period dwellings. Front setbacks are predominantly soft landscaped. Front fences are generally low and with t he style and materials generally reflecting the period of the dwellings. The dominant fences are brick, bric k and metal, and iron palisade.

Clause 9.15.1 - parking (development_control): Off street car parking for dwellings to the north of Victoria Road is either not present due to the small lot sizes  and era of housing or via rear laneway access only. In the southern end of the precinct, the larger lot sizes and later era of the housing stock means that some dwellings have access to rea r garages via side driveways.

Clause 9.15.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): The precinct is within the Eastern Channel 1 North and East sub catchments which drain to the Cooks River.

